{"input": {"region": "Europe", "measure": "average erect penis length", "unit": "cm", "question": "What is the average penis size in Europe?"}, "output": {"answer": "Clinician-measured studies of adult men generally report an average erect length of about 13-14 cm. The best-known pooled analysis is Veale et al. (2015), which combined clinician-measured data from several countries and found a mean erect length of about 13.1 cm. Self-reported figures tend to be higher, often by 1-2 cm, so they are not directly comparable. Measurement protocols also differ, for example bone-pressed versus non-bone-pressed length, and whether erection was natural or induced. European country-level estimates vary, and some country rankings come from non-clinical or self-reported sources that are less reliable.", "value": "about 13-14 cm (clinician-measured, erect)", "sources": ["Veale D et al., 2015, BJU International: systematic review and nomograms of flaccid and erect penis size", "Clinician-measured studies of men in individual European countries, published in urology journals"], "uncertainty": "Samples are often volunteers or men attending clinics, which may bias results. Protocols differ between studies. Regional differences within Europe are not well characterised by high-quality data. Many studies are over a decade old, and the pooled data are not fully representative of all European populations."}}
{"input": {"region": "Europe", "measure": "average erect penis length", "unit": "cm", "question": "What is the average penis size in Europe?"}, "output": {"answer": "Clinician-measured studies of adult men generally report an average erect penis length of about 13-14 cm. The most cited pooled estimate is Veale et al., 2015, which found a mean erect length of about 13.1 cm, measured from the pubic bone to the tip. Self-reported figures are usually higher than clinician-measured ones, so the two should not be compared directly. Protocols also differ, for example bone-pressed versus non-pressed measurement, and erection induced by drugs versus natural erection. Country-level European data are limited, and values between countries are not well established.", "value": "about 13-14 cm (erect, clinician-measured)", "sources": ["Veale D et al., 2015, BJU International: systematic review and nomogram of penile size", "Herbenick D et al., 2014, Journal of Sexual Medicine: study of self-measured penile size"], "uncertainty": "Most pooled data come from mixed regions and are not specific to Europe. Volunteer participation may bias samples toward larger sizes. Methods differ between studies and some data are more than a decade old. Differences between European countries are not reliably established."}}
{"input": {"region": "Europe", "measure": "average erect penis length", "unit": "cm", "question": "What is the average penis size in Europe?"}, "output": {"answer": "Clinician-measured studies of adult men generally report a mean erect length of about 13-14 cm. The most cited pooled analysis is Veale et al. (2015), which found a mean of about 13.1 cm (bone-pressed, clinician-measured). European country estimates vary by study, often falling between about 13 and 15 cm. Self-reported figures tend to be larger than clinician-measured ones, and measuring with or without pressing to the pubic bone changes results, so comparisons across studies should be made cautiously. Many studies measure stretched flaccid length as a proxy for erect length.", "value": "about 13-14 cm", "sources": ["Veale D et al., 2015, BJU International (systematic review and nomogram of penile size)", "Clinician-measured studies of European men, various years, urology journals"], "uncertainty": "Europe-wide figures are pooled from studies in only some countries. Samples are often volunteers or clinic patients, which may cause bias. Methods differ between studies, and some data are decades old. Regional differences within Europe are not well established."}}
{"input": {"region": "Czech Republic", "measure": "average erect penis length", "unit": "cm", "question": "What is the average dick size in Czech Republic?"}, "output": {"answer": "No large clinician-measured national study for the Czech Republic is known to me. Global pooled estimates for adult men give a mean erect length of about 13-14 cm, and Central European samples generally fall near that range. Self-reported values tend to run higher than clinician-measured ones, so the two should not be compared directly. Protocols also differ: bone-pressed versus non-pressed measurement, and stretched versus erect length, can shift results by around 1 cm.", "value": "about 13-14 cm (regional estimate, not Czech-specific)", "sources": ["Veale et al., 2015, BJU International (systematic review and nomogram of penis size)", "Wylie and Eardley, 2007, BJU International (review of penile size studies)"], "uncertainty": "No reliable Czech-specific figure is known to me. The pooled data come mostly from other countries, with sample bias, mixed methods, and differing ages of data. Regional and individual variation is considerable, so the range should be treated as approximate."}}

